Hi,

On an AMD =22Strix Halo=22 (Ryzen AI Max+ 395) mini-PC, the USB4 host sid=
e initialises correctly, but the UCSI (USB Type-C System Interface) layer=
 never comes up, so no USB4/Type-C peripheral is ever detected under Linu=
x (USB4 NVMe enclosures, eGPUs, TB4 docks). Standard USB 2.0/3.x on the s=
ame physical ports works, and the same USB4 dock works flawlessly on macO=
S =E2=80=94 so this is isolated to the UCSI/PPM software path. I'd apprec=
iate guidance on whether this is a known Strix Halo AGESA/PM=46W issue an=
d whether a kernel-side quirk is warranted.

=23=23 System under test
- Product: GEEKOM A9 Mega
- Processor: AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 (Radeon 8060S)
- BIOS: 0.13 (build 03/03/2026) EC: 0.16
- AGESA: StrixHaloPI-=46P11 1.0.0.2 PSP BL: 0.40.0.64 SMU: 10.100.06.00 M=
P2: 0B.00.00.2=46
- OS: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS Kernel: 6.18.6-061806-generic (Ubuntu mainline)
- Peripheral: GRAUGEAR G-M2DK-U4-40G (USB4 40 Gbps NVMe dock, controller =
ASMedia ASM2464PD)

=23=23 Symptom
On every plug-in of the dock to either USB4 Type-C port:
- No PD negotiation response; the dock is unpowered (LED dark, fan never =
spins).
- Linux registers no plug events: nothing in dmesg, no entries in /sys/cl=
ass/typec/, =60boltctl monitor=60 and =60udevadm monitor=60 capture nothi=
ng.
- Standard USB 2.0 / USB 3.2 Gen2 devices on the same physical port work =
normally.
- The same dock + same cable powers up instantly on an Apple Silicon Mac =
and reaches full PCIe Gen4 x4 =E2=80=94 so the dock and cable are healthy=
.

=23=23 The USB4 host controllers are fine
=24 ls /sys/bus/thunderbolt/devices/
0-0 1-0 domain0 domain1

=24 boltctl domains
=E2=97=8F domain0 security: iommu+user
=E2=97=8F domain1 security: iommu+user

=24 sudo dmesg =7C grep USB4
ACPI: USB4 =5FOSC: OS supports USB3+ DisplayPort+ PCIe+ XDomain+
ACPI: USB4 =5FOSC: OS controls USB3+ DisplayPort+ PCIe+ XDomain+

Both USB4 domains register with security iommu+user; the Thunderbolt modu=
le loads. The peripheral side is never triggered because Type-C plug dete=
ction never reaches Linux =E2=86=92 points at UCSI/PPM.

=23=23 UCSI fails, distinctly, in BOTH BIOS UCSI modes
Mode =22At MMIO=22 (UCSI Support -> Enabled -> At MMIO): ucsi=5Facpi bind=
s to USBC000:00 but the PPM reset never completes =E2=80=94 times out aft=
er =7E5.4 s:

=5B 0.003739=5D ACPI: SSDT 0x70320000 0014E4 (v02 AMD CPMUCSI 00000001 IN=
TL 20220331)
=5B 1.897156=5D WARNING: ucsi=5Freset=5Fppm+0x1a7/0x1c0 =5Btypec=5Fucsi=5D=

=5B 7.327857=5D WARNING: ucsi=5Freset=5Fppm+0x1a7/0x1c0 =5Btypec=5Fucsi=5D=

=5B 7.350046=5D ucsi=5Facpi USBC000:00: error -ETIMEDOUT: PPM init failed=


Reproduced across multiple cold boots and after a 60 s hard power drain (=
mains off, power button held) =E2=80=94 fully deterministic, not a transi=
ent PSP soft-state.

Mode =22At EC RAM=22: ucsi=5Facpi is loaded but never binds to USBC000:00=
 =E2=80=94 no init attempt, no error, no /sys/class/typec/ entries:

=24 lsmod =7C grep -iE =22ucsi=7Ctypec=22
ucsi=5Facpi 12288 0
typec=5Fucsi 69632 1 ucsi=5Facpi
typec 118784 1 typec=5Fucsi

=24 ls /sys/class/typec/
(empty)

=24 cat /sys/bus/acpi/devices/USBC000:00/modalias
acpi:USBC000:PNP0CA0:

=24 readlink /sys/bus/acpi/devices/USBC000:00/driver
(no driver bound)

The ACPI device USBC000:00 (HID PNP0CA0) is present, but ucsi=5Facpi does=
 not claim it =E2=80=94 as if the EC-RAM operations region the SBIOS expo=
ses doesn't match what mainline expects, or the =5FDSM/=5FCRS descriptor =
doesn't advertise the EC-RAM transport in a way the driver recognises.

=23=23 Possibly-relevant ACPI clue
=5B 0.003718=5D ACPI: SSDT ... (v02 AMD CPMEC 00000001 INTL 20220331)
=5B 0.003739=5D ACPI: SSDT ... (v02 AMD CPMUCSI 00000001 INTL 20220331)

The CPMUCSI SSDT is dated 20220331 (31 March 2022) =E2=80=94 earlier than=
 the Strix Halo AGESA build. It looks like the UCSI ACPI methods were car=
ried forward from an older platform reference and not refreshed for Strix=
 Halo's PPM.

=23=23 Behaviour summary
- Disabled: no ACPI device exposed; Type-C stack absent; USB4 peripheral =
not detected.
- Enabled/At MMIO: ucsi=5Facpi binds, PPM reset times out (-ETIMEDOUT); T=
ype-C absent; not detected.
- Enabled/At EC RAM: ucsi=5Facpi loaded but does not bind USBC000:00; Typ=
e-C absent; not detected.

=23=23 Questions
1. Is a PPM-init -ETIMEDOUT on Strix Halo (AGESA StrixHaloPI-=46P11 1.0.0=
.2) a known issue=3F AMD has published later StrixHaloPI-=46P11 revisions=
 (1.0.0.4, 1.1.0.0, 1.2.0.x) =E2=80=94 do any carry UCSI/PPM fixes that w=
ould resolve the MMIO PPM timeout once an OEM integrates them=3F
2. =46or the =22At EC RAM=22 mode: what does mainline ucsi=5Facpi require=
 of the EC-RAM operations region / =5FDSM to bind, and does this SBIOS's =
descriptor diverge from it=3F Is a kernel quirk feasible=3F
3. Do other Strix Halo systems (=46ramework Desktop, HP Z2 Mini G1a, GMKt=
ec EVO-X2, Beelink GTR9) bring up USBC000/CPMUCSI on the same kernel =E2=80=
=94 i.e. is this OEM-SBIOS-specific or AGESA-wide=3F

=23=23 I can provide
=46ull =60sudo dmesg=60 from cold boot under each BIOS setting, =60acpidu=
mp=60, =60lspci -vvv=60 for both USB4 domains, and =60modinfo=60 for ucsi=
=5Facpi/typec=5Fucsi. I can also test a beta/engineering BIOS on this exa=
ct unit and report back. (I have an active research collaboration with RP=
TU Kaiserslautern-Landau and am familiar with filing useful upstream bug =
reports.)

=46ull field report attached (with the macOS side-by-side and all capture=
s).

Thanks,
Stefan Walcz =E2=80=94 Walcz Strategic Consulting, Mannheim, Germany

